"_score_fcf_yield":null,"_gate_int_coverage":null,"_gp_int_coverage":null,"_score_int_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":0.0006777428465153433,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":28.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.07936337077877918,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":91.6,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.006562075092936104,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":91.8,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.031734694004921016,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":27.3,"_gate_rev_durability":0.10836831356623744,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":79.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.10737919142557892,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.06629149935934198,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.004937699217618082,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":91.8,"_gate_insider_own":0.02093,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":14.0,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Civista Bancshares, Inc. operates as the financial holding company for Civista Bank that provides banking services in the United States. The company offers personal and commercial checking accounts; retirement, money market, time, and savings accounts; safe deposit boxes; wire transfers; and automated teller services. It also provides internet banking; ACH origination; telephone banking; and mobile/digital banking services, as well as remote deposit capture banking services for retail and business customers. In addition, the company offers time deposits that consist of certificates of deposit, including those held in IRA accounts and reciprocal deposits. Further, its loan portfolio includes commercial and agriculture; commercial real estate \u0096 owner and non-owner occupied; residential and farm real estate; real estate construction; lease financing receivable; consumer; and other loans, as well as home equity line of credit. Additionally, the company holds and manages securities portfolio; leases general equipment; and provides captive insurance products and investment advisory services. It operates in North Central, West Central, South Western Ohio, South Eastern Indiana, and Northern Kentucky. The company was formerly known as First Citizens Banc Corp and changed its name to Civista Bancshares, Inc. in May 2015. Civista Bancshares, Inc. was founded in 1884 and is headquartered in Sandusky, Ohio.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Charles A. Parcher | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $595,040 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 550 people. Revenue per employee of $314K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 9%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $77K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Civista Bancshares, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $593M market cap on $173M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years and +11% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 11% against a 8% cost of capital, a 3-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $42M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, with adequate 0.94\u00d7 cash conversion.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 10.7% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 2.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 39% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons bu